studio: fm, the thing at its cursor in ed, and a shell
  Lines stack down, the lines under one go across, and the lines under
  those down again. Each line is a slot, and a share such as 70% is its
  part of its parent; the rest of the line is what runs in it, and a
  slot that names nothing keeps a shell. fm -f and ed -f follow cur, so
  ed edits whatever fm's cursor is on, and both go where a click
  anywhere says; a slot that runs studio show adds the lenses, diff,
  figure and run. A slot's name is how a program reaches it: studio send
  shell make pastes make into the shell, and studio read shell reads it;
  e opens a text in ed, o a folder in fm, and a middle click hands a word
  to shell (design/mouse). fm's slot is the frame's face: its q ends the
  frame, asking first while ed holds work unsaved; q in ed or a lens
  ends nothing, and a shell that exits ends alone.
top     70%
  fm    40%  fm -f
  ed         ed -f
shell
